  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the whole game in `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so none of it has been run or looked at on screen.\n\n- **Scene:** The scene uses the `neon-arcade` look, a fixed perspective camera and a 3×3 grid of pedestals with dark holes. Each cell has a lantern and a bomb object (built from primitives with emissive materials) that rise and sink. A cyan hover ring and a red miss ring are scene nodes. Gold and red spark pools give the pop, miss and bomb bursts.\n- **Picking:** Clicks are resolved with my own ray test against the known camera. A raised object counts as a hit, a lowered or empty cell costs 5, and the gaps between cells are ignored.\n- **Rules:**\n  - A raised lantern pops for +10.\n  - A bomb ends the run as `lost`.\n  - A 45 s timer ends the round as `won` at 150 points or more, otherwise `lost`.\n  - Lanterns stay up for less time as the score rises.\n  - Spawns come from a seeded mulberry32 generator that is reset to the same seed on every round. The seed is 20240607 unless you pass `?seed=`.\n  - Logic runs on a fixed 1/60 s step.\n- **Controls:** The game starts as `ready`. Start or Enter begins a round. R or the Restart button begins a new one.\n- **HUD:** The DOM HUD sits below the canvas with ids `hud-score`, `hud-time` and `hud-status`. The overlay is positioned over the canvas and shows the Start or Restart button.\n- **State and ready flag:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` holds `status`, `score`, `timeLeft` and `activeCells`. `window.__TASK_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` resolves and two animation frames have run.\n- **Not in the task:** I added `window.__TASK_CELL_CENTERS__`, which holds the on-canvas pixel position of each raised object, for anyone driving the game with clicks.\n\n",
